      "side": 1,
      "message": "I reread the thread and I guess BlobCache is kind of the place where std::byte is sort of reasonable. BlobCache treats it as opaque bytes and does do much of anything with the data other than copying it. Using span\u003cuint8_t\u003e feels more easier to me but that also what I\u0027m used to so I\u0027ll leave that up to Dawn folks to decide.\n\nI left a couple suggestions on the first part of the CL but I\u0027ll hold off looking at the rest until byte vs uint8_t is settled.",
