      "message": "I\u0027m pretty skeptical these functions are a good idea. At least for the real span  using `blob.Data().begin()` seems better. Really with std::ranges you\u0027ll be passing the whole span instead of begin/end iterators most of the time like `std::ranges::copy(blob.Data(), ...)`\n\nFor the conversion to an arbitrary T span it seems like it\u0027s just used for copying. We can convert the other span to `std::span\u003cbyte\u003e` or `std::span\u003cuint8_T\u003e` for the same effect eg. `std::ranges::copy(std::as_bytes(data), blob.Data().begin())`",
